==English==

===Etymology===
{{back-form|liaison|nodot=1}}, itself from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|liaison||binding|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|ligatio|lang=la}} (stem ''ligation-'') (English {{term|ligation|lang=en}}), derived from {{term|ligo|ligō||I bind|lang=la}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|leygʰ-|to bind|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/liːeɪz/}}
* {{rhymes|eɪz}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|liais|ing}}

# To establish a [[liaison]].
# To act between parties with a view to reconciling differences.
# To cooperate, consult and discuss in order to come to a common solution.

